      "description": "Watch River Plate vs Barracas Central highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 26, 2026. The Liga Profesional Argentina served up a compelling encounter on July 26, 2026, as River Plate locked horns with Barracas Central . Both sides took to the pitch with high expectations, setting the stage for a match where discipline and clinical finishing would prove to be the deciding factors. Morales Breaks the Deadlock The match ignited in the 22nd minute when the visitors found their rhythm in the final third. Lautaro Pereyra turned provider, delivering a precise ball to Gonzalo Morales , who made no mistake in finding the back of the net. This opening goal shifted the momentum, forcing the hosts to increase their attacking output while Barracas Central sat back to absorb the pressure. As the first half drew to a close, the physical nature of the contest intensified. The referee was kept busy, issuing yellow cards to Kevin Jappert and Ezequiel Centurion during a heated period of play. The halftime whistle offered a much-needed breather for both sets of players after a grueling opening 45 minutes. A Battle of Attrition in the Second Half The second period began with tactical adjustments, as River Plate introduced Lucas Beltran and Joaquin Freitas to spark a comeback. However, the game became increasingly fragmented due to a series of fouls and cautions. Norberto Briasco , Mauro Arambarri , and Jhonatan Candia were all cautioned as the battle for supremacy in midfield turned fierce. Despite late efforts from River Plate , including the introduction of Angel Correa , the Barracas Central defense remained resolute. Further bookings for Dardo Federico Miloc and Ivan Guaraz highlighted the desperate nature of the closing stages. After seven minutes of stoppage time, the final whistle confirmed a hard-earned victory for the visiting side, leaving the home fans frustrated by a lack of breakthrough."
